---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "Wire Mesh for Construction: Reinforcement, Formwork & Safety Applications";
const description = "Guide to wire mesh in building construction. Covers concrete reinforcement, plaster mesh, safety barriers, and scaffolding applications with sourcing tips.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Wire Mesh in Construction</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-2xl">
        Beyond concrete reinforcement, wire mesh serves multiple roles in modern
        construction—from plaster backing to safety barriers. Understanding each
        application helps optimize material selection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-amber-500">Home</a> / 
    <span>Applications</span> / 
    Construction
  </nav>

  <article class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <!-- Overview -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Construction Applications Overview</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        Wire mesh appears throughout the construction process, from foundation to finish:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Concrete reinforcement</strong> — Slabs, walls, precast elements (see <a href="/applications/concrete/" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline">dedicated guide</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>Plaster/stucco mesh</strong> — Crack prevention under render and stucco</li>
        <li><strong>Masonry reinforcement</strong> — Wall ties, ladder reinforcement, bed joint reinforcement</li>
        <li><strong>Safety barriers</strong> — Edge protection, debris netting, guardrails</li>
        <li><strong>Scaffolding</strong> — Work platforms, toe boards, enclosure screens</li>
        <li><strong>Gabions</strong> — Retaining walls, erosion control, architectural features</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Plaster Mesh -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Plaster & Stucco Mesh</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        Wire mesh under plaster and stucco prevents cracking from thermal movement
        and substrate irregularities:
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Expanded Metal Lath</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Diamond-pattern expanded steel with integral ribs. Traditional choice for
            stucco and render. Provides strong key for mortar.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>+ Superior mortar key</li>
            <li>+ Self-furring options available</li>
            <li>− Heavier, more expensive</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Welded Wire Mesh</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Lightweight welded mesh (typically 25-50mm aperture). Economical for
            large areas and less demanding applications.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>+ Economical, lightweight</li>
            <li>+ Easy to cut and fit</li>
            <li>− Less effective mortar key</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        <strong>Galvanizing requirement:</strong> Exterior applications require hot-dip
        galvanized mesh (minimum Z275 or equivalent) to prevent rust staining through finish.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Masonry Reinforcement -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Masonry Reinforcement</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        Wire mesh reinforces block and brick walls against cracking:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Ladder reinforcement</strong> — Two longitudinal wires with cross wires, placed in horizontal mortar joints. Standard widths: 50mm, 75mm, 100mm.</li>
        <li><strong>Truss reinforcement</strong> — Diagonal cross wires forming truss shape. Greater stiffness for longer spans.</li>
        <li><strong>Wall ties</strong> — Connect cavity wall leaves, typically 3-5mm diameter galvanized wire.</li>
        <li><strong>Bed joint reinforcement</strong> — Continuous mesh in mortar beds over openings and at floor levels.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        Standards: ASTM A951 for masonry joint reinforcement, local building codes
        for spacing and placement requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Safety Applications -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Safety & Temporary Works</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">
        Construction sites use wire mesh for worker protection and debris containment:
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Edge Protection</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Guardrail systems with welded mesh infill panels. Prevents falls and
            dropped objects. Typically 1.1m height with toe board.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Debris Netting</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Fine mesh screens attached to scaffolding. Contains dust, debris, and
            tools. Fire-retardant options for hot work areas.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Scaffold Enclosures</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Weather protection and containment screens. Allows work to continue in
            adverse conditions while protecting public below.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Temporary Fencing</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Construction site perimeter security. Chain link or welded panels on
            temporary posts. See <a href="/applications/fence/" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline">fence guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Material Standards -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Material Standards for Construction</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Application</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Standard</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Key Requirement</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Concrete reinforcement</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">ASTM A1064</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Weld shear strength, yield strength</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Masonry reinforcement</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">ASTM A951</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Wire diameter, spacing, coating</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Plaster lath</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">ASTM C847</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Weight, rib height, coating</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Safety barriers</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">OSHA/EN standards</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">Load capacity, height, mesh size</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sourcing -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Sourcing Construction Mesh</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-4">
        <div class="border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Bundle by application</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Different construction meshes often come from different factory types.
            Concrete reinforcement from heavy mesh producers; plaster mesh from lighter
            mesh specialists. Consider separate sourcing for optimal pricing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Verify coating specifications</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            "Galvanized" ranges from electroplated (thin, indoor only) to hot-dip
            (thick, outdoor). Specify coating weight (g/m²) or ASTM coating class.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Plan for site storage</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
            Mesh arrives in compact bundles or rolls. Ensure dry storage to prevent
            premature rusting, especially for uncoated or lightly coated products.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Pages -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Continue Exploring</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/applications/concrete/" class="block p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded hover:border-amber-500 transition">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Wire Mesh for Concrete</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Detailed WWR specifications and standards</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/applications/fence/" class="block p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded hover:border-amber-500 transition">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Wire Mesh Fence</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Temporary and permanent fencing solutions</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/products/welded-wire-mesh/" class="block p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded hover:border-amber-500 transition">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Welded Wire Mesh</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Construction-grade welded mesh specs</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/products/gabion-baskets/" class="block p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded hover:border-amber-500 transition">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Gabion Baskets</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Retaining walls and erosion control</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded p-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Need Construction Mesh?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">Send your project specifications. We'll connect you with qualified manufacturers.</p>
      <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-400 text-slate-900 font-semibold px-6 py-2 rounded transition">
        Send Inquiry
      </a>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
